# Signed material must never be line-ending normalised: it moves the file hash
# without changing the content, and a published hash then cannot be reproduced.
*.asc -text
*.sig -text
*.docx -text
*.md -text

# MANIFEST.sha256 is the file MANIFEST.sha256.asc signs and MANIFEST.sha256.ots
# timestamps. Normalising its line endings on checkout would move its hash, and both
# the signature and the timestamp would then fail to verify against the copy the
# reader holds - on Windows, for a reason that has nothing to do with the content.
# The .ots proof is binary and must not be touched at all.
*.sha256 -text
*.ots -text -diff
